#🛒 ShopVista E-Commerce Data Pipeline — Azure End-to-End

## 📌 Project Overview
An end-to-end data engineering pipeline built on Azure, processing raw e-commerce transactional data from the ShopVista OLTP system into analytics-ready Gold layer tables using the Medallion Architecture (Bronze → Silver → Gold).
The pipeline handles both historical full loads (Jan 2024 – Aug 2025) and daily incremental ingestion (Aug 2025 – Dec 2025), with governance managed through Unity Catalog.

## 🏗️ Architecture
ShopVista (OLTP)
      │
      ▼ CSV
Azure Data Lake Storage (ADLS)
      │
      ▼ Access Connector (Secure Access)
Azure Databricks + Unity Catalog
      │
      ├──▶ Bronze Layer  (Raw ingestion — Delta tables)
      │
      ├──▶ Silver Layer  (Cleaned & validated — Delta tables)
      │
      └──▶ Gold Layer    (Business-ready aggregations — Delta tables)
                │
                ▼
           Power BI (Analytics & Reporting)

Full architecture diagram:





## 📦 Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Cloud Storage** | Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 (ADLS) | Scalable cloud-based data storage |
| **Processing** | Azure Databricks (PySpark, SQL) | Distributed ETL and big data processing |
| **Streaming Ingestion** | Auto Loader (`cloudFiles`) + Structured Streaming | Incremental and real-time data ingestion |
| **Table Format** | Delta Lake | ACID transactions, Time Travel, and Change Data Feed (CDF) |
| **Governance** | Unity Catalog | Centralized governance using Catalog → Schema → Tables |
| **Orchestration** | Databricks Jobs & Pipelines | Scheduled daily workflow execution and refresh |
| **Reporting** | Power BI | Interactive dashboards and business reporting |
| **Languages** | Python (PySpark), SQL | Data engineering and transformation logic |



📂 Data Model
Source Tables (ShopVista)
Dimension Tables (historical full load)

brands, category, products, customers, date

Fact Tables (incremental daily load from Aug 2025)

order_items, order_returns, order_shipments

Medallion Layers
ecommerce (catalog)
├── raw          → External volume pointing to ADLS raw landing zone
├── bronze       → brz_brands, brz_categories, brz_products,
│                  brz_customers, brz_dates, brz_order_items
├── silver       → slv_brands, slv_category, slv_products,
│                  slv_customers, slv_order_items
└── gold         → gld_dim_products, gld_dim_customers,
                   gld_fact_order_items, gld_fact_daily_orders_summary

🔄 Pipeline Details
1. Bronze Layer — Raw Ingestion
Dimension tables are ingested from raw CSV files stored in ADLS into Delta tables with:

Defined PySpark schema per table
Metadata columns: _source_file, ingested_at (for lineage and auditing)
Write mode: overwrite with schema merge

Fact tables are ingested using Auto Loader (Structured Streaming):

cloudFiles format for incremental file detection
Schema inference and evolution enabled
_rescued_data column captures unexpected schema changes safely
Checkpointing for fault-tolerance and exactly-once processing
Append mode into ecommerce.bronze.brz_order_items


2. Silver Layer — Cleansing & Transformation
Dimension cleansing:

Trimming whitespace from string columns
Removing special characters from identifier fields
Standardizing inconsistent category codes via replacement dictionary
Deduplication using groupBy() + dropDuplicates()

Fact cleansing (order_items):

Converting text numerics (e.g., "Two" → 2)
Stripping $ and % symbols from price/discount columns
Normalizing coupon_code (trim + lowercase)
Standardizing channel values (web → Website, app → Mobile)
Adding processed_time for transformation tracking

Incremental upsert strategy using Structured Streaming + foreachBatch:

Delta Lake MERGE (upsert) on composite key (order_id, item_seq)
Change Data Feed (CDF) enabled on Silver fact table
Checkpointing for recovery


3. Gold Layer — Business-Ready Tables
Dimension enrichment:

gld_dim_products: Joined product + brand + category; COALESCE for null handling
gld_dim_customers: Country–state–region mapping via PySpark dictionary join, deriving region attribute

Fact aggregation (order_items → Gold):
Derived metrics:

gross_amount = quantity × unit_price
discount_amount = derived from discount_pct
net_amount = gross_amount − discount_amount + tax
coupon_flag = boolean indicator for coupon usage

Incremental load via Structured Streaming + foreachBatch with CDF on Silver (processes insert and update_postimage only).
Daily Summary Table (gld_fact_daily_orders_summary):

Aggregates total quantity, gross amount, discount, tax, net sales by date_id and currency
Dynamic filter: last N days for incremental refresh
Delta MERGE upsert on subsequent runs; auto clustering for query optimization


4. Orchestration
JobTriggerNotebooksdaily_refresh_dimScheduled dailyDimension Bronze → Silver → Golddaily_refresh_factScheduled dailyFact Bronze → Silver → Golddaily_refresh_allScheduled dailyCombined dim + fact pipeline

5. Governance (Unity Catalog)

Access Connector set up for secure ADLS access from Databricks
External Location configured for raw data volume
Catalog → Schema → Tables structure enforced across all layers
Data access control and metadata management via Unity Catalog


